## SERIAL PROTOCOL (ground truth — never change without updating docs)

### Device → Host (one JSON per line, `\n` terminated, 115200 baud)

**Sample frame:**
```json
{
  "ts": 12345,        // uint32, uptime ms
  "n":  42,           // uint32, sequence number
  "ch0": 12.3401,     // float, raw capacitance pF channel 0
  "ch1": 12.1003,     // float, raw capacitance pF channel 1
  "ch2": 11.9812,     // float, raw capacitance pF channel 2
  "ch3": 12.0540,     // float, raw capacitance pF channel 3
  "d0": 0.0021,       // float, delta from baseline pF ch0
  "d1": -0.0132,      // float, delta from baseline pF ch1
  "d2": 0.0088,       // float, delta from baseline pF ch2
  "d3": -0.0044,      // float, delta from baseline pF ch3
  "temp": 28.5,       // float, temperature °C (-99 if unavailable)
  "bat_mv": 3820,     // uint32, battery mV
  "mp_index": 0.00821,// float, RMS delta = sqrt(mean(di^2))
  "mode": "sample"    // string, always "sample" for data frames
}
```

**Status frames:**
```json
{"status": "boot",            "fw": "nira-v1.1", "proto": "nira-serial-v1"}
{"status": "zeroing"}
{"status": "zero_done",       "base_pF": [12.34, 12.10, 11.98, 12.05]}
{"status": "ready"}
{"status": "streaming_start"}
{"status": "streaming_stop"}
{"status": "resetting"}
{"status": "rate_set",        "interval_ms": 500}
```

**Error frames:**
```json
{"error": "sensor_read_failed"}
{"error": "unknown_cmd", "cmd": "..."}
{"error": "invalid_rate"}
```

### Host → Device (ASCII, `\n` terminated)

| Command        | Effect                                  |
|----------------|-----------------------------------------|
| `CMD:START`    | Resume streaming                        |
| `CMD:STOP`     | Pause streaming                         |
| `CMD:ZERO`     | Re-capture baseline (32-sample average) |
| `CMD:RATE:<ms>`| Set sample interval (50–60000 ms)       |
| `CMD:RESET`    | Software restart                        |

