## FOSS HACK 2026 COMPLIANCE CHECKLIST

Before every commit, verify ALL of these:

### Licensing
- [ ] All `.cpp` and `.h` files have GPL-3.0 SPDX header: `// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later`
- [ ] All `.py` files have GPL-3.0 SPDX header: `# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later`
- [ ] `LICENSE.md` is present and correct
- [ ] Hardware files have CERN-OHL-P-2.0 header
- [ ] `README.md` shows all three license badges

### No Proprietary Dependencies
- [ ] Zero npm/pip packages with proprietary licenses
- [ ] No Google Fonts CDN calls
- [ ] No API keys or cloud endpoints anywhere in the codebase
- [ ] `nira_gui.py` runs 100% offline after `pip install`
- [ ] Firmware compiles without internet access (all libs in `lib_deps` are cached)

### Documentation
- [ ] `README.md` has: project description, hardware list, wiring table, install steps, usage, license table
- [ ] `docs/SERIAL_PROTOCOL.md` is current with `main.cpp`
- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` has an entry for this change
- [ ] All functions have docstrings/Doxygen

### Reproducibility
- [ ] `platformio.ini` pins all library versions with `@`
- [ ] Python deps listed in `requirements.txt` with pinned versions
- [ ] Hardware BOM is in `hardware/v1.0_esp32_sensor/BOM.csv`

### Community
- [ ] `CONTRIBUTING.md` exists
- [ ] Issues/PRs use GitHub templates (`.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`)

